{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Liam jolted awake to the sharp beep of his alarm, but something felt wrong. The digital clock displayed **00:00**, and sunlight poured through a window he didn’t remember installing—thick glass panels framed a sky that stretched too perfectly, like a painted backdrop. His fingers ghosted over the mattress, but the fabric was too smooth, too *digital*; his reflection in the dresser mirror flickered like a low-resolution render. When he pinched his arm, the pain registered, but his skin didn’t dimple—just rippled like a texture error. His phone, plugged in and fully charged despite him never unplugging it, buzzed with a notification: **\"Tutorial Objective: Discover Your Abilities\"** in neon-blue lettering. Outside, a stranger in a trench coat eyed him from across the street; when Liam blinked, the man vanished into a glitching void of static.\n\nLiam sprinted to the window, heart hammering, but the view outside warped into a pixelated battlefield—enemies with health bars and floating loot crates materialized in the park below. A dialogue box popped up: **\"You are now PLAYER. Choose your class: Warrior, Mage, or Rogue.\"** His hands trembled as he hovered over the options, but before he could click, his reflection reached out and grabbed his shoulder. When he turned, no one was there—just empty air and the faint sound of a developer’s voice whispering, *\"Stay awhile and play.\"* The first enemy’s attack bar filled in red as it lunged. Liam’s fingers finally moved, selecting **Rogue**, and the world dissolved into a loading screen—this time, with the words **\"CONTINUE?\"** glowing in the dark.", "logprobs": [{"token": "L", "logprob": -1.2783106565475464}, {"token": "iam", "logprob": -0.035093605518341064}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.8107053637504578}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0011453027836978436}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -2.181